// Linux half of the `bit_rt_host_target` port (#1635). See
// ../roothostdarwin/roothostdarwin.bit for why the VALUE needs a running proof
// that `rootpins` cannot give, and for the expiry date on the seed oracle.
//
// The Linux provider is the interesting one: it must separate x86_64-linux (0)
// from aarch64-linux (1), a distinction the `{linux,darwin}` directory split
// does NOT draw. It draws it with an `asm` block's per-arch sub-blocks (SPEC
// §11.6) — one immediate move, selected by the backend at codegen, exactly
// `runtime/sched/sched.bit`'s `entryBias` shape and for the same reason: an
// inline immediate is not an `ir.RtFn` call, so it cannot become the self-call
// that #1583's rename would make of `return hostTarget()`.
//
// THE GOLDEN CANNOT NAME THE ORDINAL, because one `.expected` serves both Linux
// arches and the correct answers differ (0 vs 1) — that is the whole point of
// the mechanism. So the assertions are arch-free:
//   - `seedAgrees`: the ported provider equals the still-Zig `hostTarget()`
//     primitive, which reads Zig's compile-time `builtin.target`. This is the
//     one that pins the exact value per arch, and it is why a swapped pair of
//     immediates (x64 -> 1, arm64 -> 0) reddens this test on BOTH arches rather
//     than neither.
//   - `isLinux`: the answer is in {0, 1}, i.e. the provider never reports the
//     Darwin ordinal from a Linux archive. This survives #1584, when
//     `seedAgrees` becomes tautological.
// The per-arch ordinal itself is verified by running this program on each arch
// (#1635 ran both under `docker run --rm`) and by disassembling the emitted
// `bit_rt_root_host_target`.
//
// `linux-only`: the imported provider uses raw `syscall` (§11.8), which a Darwin
// target rejects outright, so this neither compiles nor runs on macOS.

import { rtHostTarget } from "../../../runtime/root/linux"

fn main() {
  let ordinal = rtHostTarget()
  let seedAgrees = ordinal == hostTarget()
  let isLinux = ordinal == 0 || ordinal == 1

  print("roothostlinux seedAgrees=${seedAgrees} isLinux=${isLinux}\n")
}
